From 26f1396306cfd742d109fbe8769d571d5e578100 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Stewart <peter@stewartmail.xyz>
Date: Sat, 21 Feb 2026 18:13:39 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] wineusb0.sys: Add generic libusb-win32 compatibility
 driver.

Bridge libusb-win32 (v1.2.6 ABI) IOCTLs to Linux libusb, allowing
Windows applications that use libusb-win32 to access USB devices.

Devices are exposed as \\.\libusb0-XXXX and support the standard
libusb-win32 control/bulk/vendor IOCTLs. Device handles are opened
lazily on IRP_MJ_CREATE (rather than at hotplug time) to avoid holding
libusb handles to every USB device on the system.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 41bfbb355f687c34cb8fe4c293d09650d91d40cd)
